{{Quote|Despite some exceptions, little is known about the Xi'Dec (like many other insectoid species).|"Species From A to Z"|<ref name="Species From A to Z" />}}
The '''Xi'Dec''' were an [[insectoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]<ref name="TLJVD" /> from [[Stic]].<ref name="Species From A to Z" /> [[Ubbla Mollbro]], a [[Gender|female]] [[opera]] singer with engorged egg sacs, was a member of this species.<ref name="TLJVD" />

==Xi'Dec in the galaxy==
During the [[New Republic Era]], [[Captain]] [[Carson Teva]] sent out the survival compendium "[[Species From A to Z]]," which included an entry on the Xi'Dec [[species]].<ref name="Species From A to Z" /> Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="SC Date">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> [[Bubbles (individual)|Bubbles]] ,a [[Gender|female]] Xi'Dec, was a guest at the [[Skull Ridge Mountain Hotel & Spa]] on the [[planet]] [[Lanupa]].<ref name="SC 106">{{SkeletonCrew|Zero Friends Again}}</ref> The opera singer [[Ubbla Mollbro]] spent time in the city [[Canto Bight]] on the planet [[Cantonica]] in search for a potential partner.<ref name="Species From A to Z" />

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], the Xi'Dec were first described in ''[[Galaxy Guide 4: Alien Races]]'', a supplement for ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]'' written by [[Troy Denning]] and published by [[West End Games]] in [[1989]].<ref name="Galaxy Guide 4">''[[Galaxy Guide 4: Alien Races]]''</ref> The species was made [[canon]] when it appeared in the [[sequel trilogy]] film {{Film|VIII}}, released on [[December 15]], [[2017]].<ref name="VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

In Legends, the Xi'Dec had at least 180 different sexes and [[Reproduction|reproduced]] in a variety of different ways.<ref name="Galaxy Guide 4" /> It is currently unknown if this is also true for canon Xi'Dec or if they all share Ubbla's biology and reproduce through eggs.<ref name="TLJVD" />

